closed	p2	Bot commands risk Discord's 3-second 'application did not respond' timeout: no response deferral anywhere. lightbulb v3 does NOT auto-defer (v2 had an auto_defer= command option, but this bot never used it - commands have been class-based v3 style since d38aeff). The bot calls ctx.defer() nowhere and registers no auto-defer hook, so any command doing backend-API or Discord-REST I/O BEFORE its first ctx.respond() can exceed Discord's 3s interaction window. At risk: /judge (does fetch_channel + create_message REST calls before the first respond - highest risk), and the AUTHED paths of /setup, /report, /sanction, /register, /checkin (call fetch_userinfo against the backend before responding). The new-user / OAuth-link paths respond instantly (local sqlite get_tokens only) so they are safe - which is why #91 §6 step 4's first /setup hit won't time out. FIX: add a global AUTO_DEFER execution step that defers EPHEMERALLY (lightbulb.ExecutionStep('AUTO_DEFER') + client_from_app(execution_step_order=[AUTO_DEFER, *lightbulb.DEFAULT_EXECUTION_STEP_ORDER]) + @lightbulb.hook(AUTO_DEFER) calling ctx.defer(ephemeral=True), attached via hooks=[...] on each command or a shared base), OR call await ctx.defer(ephemeral=True) atop the slow commands. Ephemeral defer keeps the existing flags=EPHEMERAL follow-ups ephemeral; a non-ephemeral defer would leak them public. Needs bot wheel rebuild + re-release + redeploy. Surfaced in the #91 §6 lightbulb v2->v3 completeness audit. NOT a #91-close criterion (the path tested first responds fast). relates:#91 relates:#171
